title: The <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ z_party_name +]**</span> leaves the coalition!
subtitle: As expected.
new-page: true
on-arrival: tried_supporting_kpd = 0; z_relation -= 5; dvp_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 5; lvp_relation -= 5
view-if: chancellor_party == "SPD" and spd_in_government = 1 and federal_coalition_trigger == time and last_election_time != time
tags: event
go-to: vonc_menu

= The <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ z_party_name +]**</span> leaves the coalition!

Due to the formation of the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ z_party_name +]**</span>, our coalition is no more! [? if not constructive_vonc: They have also called for a vote of no confidence against us. ?]It's joever...

@vonc_menu

- @social_liberal_coalition: Can we form a <span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span>-[? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Liberal</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Liberal</span>?] Coalition?
- @support_kpd: Could we get the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> to abstain?
- @let_it_happen: Let the vote happen.
- @bruning_vonc: The <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ z_party_name +]**</span> calls for a constructive vote of no confidence against us!
- @support_kpd_left: Could we form a United Left coalition with the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span>?
- @spd_majority: We have a majority without them.
- @no_vonc: They cannot call a vote of no confidence due to the constitutional reforms, but they can obstruct our government at every opportunity.

@social_liberal_coalition
title: We can form a <span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span>-[? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Liberal</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Liberal</span>?] Coalition.
subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> + [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed:<span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>?] ([+ social_liberal_coalition +]%)
view-if: social_liberal_coalition >= 50 and liberal_parliament == 0 and bourgeois_parliament_ddp == 0 and cvp_formed
unavailable-subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">SPD</span> + [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>?][? if lvp_formed:<span style="color: #FFCC00;">LVP</span>?] ([+ social_liberal_coalition +]%) [? if not ((ddp_relation >= 65 and ddp_ideology == "Right") or (ddp_relation >= 55 and ddp_ideology == "Moderate") or (ddp_relation >= 45 and ddp_ideology == "Left")) and not lvp_formed: - We do not have the adequate relations with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>. ?] [? if not ((lvp_relation >= 75 and lvp_ideology == "Right") or (lvp_relation >= 65 and lvp_ideology == "Moderate") or (lvp_relation >= 55 and lvp_ideology == "Left")) and lvp_formed: - We do not have adequate relations with the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> ?]
choose-if: ((((ddp_relation >= 65 and ddp_ideology == "Right") or (ddp_relation >= 55 and ddp_ideology == "Moderate") or (ddp_relation >= 45 and ddp_ideology == "Left")) and not lvp_formed) or (((lvp_relation >= 75 and lvp_ideology == "Right") or (lvp_relation >= 65 and lvp_ideology == "Moderate") or (lvp_relation >= 55 and lvp_ideology == "Left")) and lvp_formed))
on-arrival: leverage = spd_r
go-to: election_1928.social_liberal_coalition_cvp

@support_kpd
choose-if: (in_grand_coalition and communist_coalition >= 3 and kpd_relation >= 50 and popular_front_coalition >= 50) or (in_weimar_coalition and kpd_relation >= 50 and left_coalition >= 50 and communist_coalition >= 3)
view-if: tried_supporting_kpd = 0 and not constructive_vonc
on-arrival: tried_supporting_kpd = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if communist_coalition < 3 : The <span style="color: #700000;">KPD</span> won't take part in parliamentary government. ?] [? if kpd_relation < 50 : The <span style="color: #700000;">KPD</span> is not friendly enough with us. ?] [? if (left_coalition < 50 and in_weimar_coalition) or (popular_front_coalition < 50 and in_grand_coalition): The <span style="color: #700000;">KPD</span> does not have enough votes. ?] [? if in_popular_front : We are already in a Popular Front with the <span style="color: #700000;">KPD</span>. ?]

If the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span> abstain, then we essentially can maintain a minority government[? if president=="Hindenburg":, although it would be very difficult to make policy without the support of President Hindenburg, which we do not have ?]. If this happens, then we will own a massive debt to the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span>. This could lead to broader cooperation in the future, for better or for worse.

- @support_kpd_2: Persuade the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> to "tolerate" us?
- @let_it_happen: Never mind. Let the vote happen.

@support_kpd_2
on-arrival: communist_coalition += 1; workers_kpd += 3; kpd_relation += 5; kpd_nazi_urgency += 0 if kpd_nazi_urgency < 0;
go-to: support_kpd_weimar if in_weimar_coalition; support_kpd_grand if in_grand_coalition


The <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> is not interested in a "toleration" arrangement; they will only support us if they can participate in the government as part of a coalition. And, if this toleration agreement happens, the right-wing parties will not be inclined to support us. 

@support_kpd_grand
on-arrival: support_kpd_grand = 1

- @election_1928.popular_front_coalition: Form a "Popular Front" coalition?
- @election_1928.left_coalition
- @let_it_happen: Never mind. Let the vote happen.

@support_kpd_weimar
on-arrival: support_kpd_weimar = 1

- @election_1928.left_coalition
- @let_it_happen: Never mind. Let the vote happen.


@let_it_happen
view-if: not constructive_vonc and spd_r < 50
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; spd_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_popular_front = 0; spd_toleration = 0; spd_toleration_right = 0; foreign_minister_party = "DVP"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Z"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "DVP"; finance_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"; labor_minister = "Stegerwald"; interior_minister = "Wirth"; finance_minister = "Moldenhauer"; economic_minister = "Curtius"; justice_minister = "Koch-Weser"; foreign_minister = "Stresemann" if not stresemann_dead; foreign_minister = "Curtius" if stresemann_dead; agriculture_minister = "Dietrich"; reichswehr_minister = "Groener"; z_coalition_dissent = 0; ddp_coalition_dissent = 0; dvp_coalition_dissent = 0; lvp_coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 4; old_middle_spd -= 3; new_middle_spd -= 2; workers_spd -= 3 if pro_republic < 50; workers_spd -= 4 if pro_republic < 40; old_middle_nsdap += 4 if pro_republic < 50; new_middle_nsdap += 3 if pro_republic < 50
go-to: let_it_happen_hindenburg if president_ideology != "Left"; let_it_happen_braun if president_ideology == "Left"

@let_it_happen_hindenburg
on-arrival: chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z"; welfare -= 2; bruning_event_timer = 6 if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930
go-to: elections if bruning_event_seen or year < 1930

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Chancellor Brüning has been appointed as the head of a new cabinet, consisting solely of the bourgeois parties. He immediately proceeds to cut welfare spending substantially.

[? if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930: New elections haven't been called yet but it's likely that they will be soon, considering Brüning most likely doesn't have the majority of the Reichstag behind him. ?]

@elections
call: set_next_election_time

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@let_it_happen_braun
on-arrival: spd_caretaker = 1
call: set_next_election_time

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] remains as the head of a caretaker government, but no longer has the power to enact new policies.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@bruning_vonc
view-if: constructive_vonc and center_right_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: center_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5; spd_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; z_coalition_dissent = 0; ddp_coalition_dissent = 0; dvp_coalition_dissent = 0; lvp_coalition_dissent = 0;
go-to: election_1928.right_coalition_2 if right_coalition >= 50; election_1928.center_right_coalition_2 if right_coalition < 50

@support_kpd_left
subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> [? if sapd_formed: + <span style="color: #9B0000;">**SAPD**</span> ?] ([+ left_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">SPD</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">KPD</span> [? if sapd_formed: + <span style="color: #9B0000;">SAPD</span> ?] ([+ left_coalition +]%). [? if kpd_relation < 50 : We do not have adequate relations with the <span style="color: #700000;">KPD</span>. ?][? if communist_coalition < 3 : The <span style="color: #700000;">Communists</span> are too committed to their radical ways to partake in government. ?] [? if rubicon: - Why the hell would Hindenburg allow this? ?] [? if president_ideology != "Left" and president != "Hindenburg": - President [+ president +] is fiercely opposed to <span style="color: #9B0000;">socialist</span> governance. ?]
view-if: constructive_vonc
choose-if: left_coalition >= 50 and (kpd_relation >= 50 or (kpd_leader == "Conciliators" and kpd_relation >= 40)) and communist_coalition >= 3 and not rubicon and president_ideology == "Left" or president == "Hindenburg"
go-to: election_1928.left_coalition_success

@spd_majority
view-if: spd_r >= 50
on-arrival: in_popular_front = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_social_catholic_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; foreign_minister_party = "SPD"; foreign_minister = "Breitscheid"; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; interior_minister = "Severing"; justice_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister = "Radbruch"; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; labor_minister = "Wissell"; reichswehr_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_minister = "Leber"; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; finance_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister = "Hilferding"; agriculture_minister_party = "SPD"; agriculture_minister = "Baade"; in_spd_majority = 1

We were so kind.

@no_vonc
view-if: constructive_vonc and spd_r < 50 and center_right_coalition < 50
on-arrival: in_popular_front = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_social_catholic_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_minority_government = 1; foreign_minister_party = "SPD"; foreign_minister = "Breitscheid"; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; interior_minister = "Severing"; justice_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister = "Radbruch"; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; labor_minister = "Wissell"; reichswehr_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_minister = "Leber"; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; finance_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister = "Hilferding"; agriculture_minister_party = "SPD"; agriculture_minister = "Baade"

We have been effectively made a minority government, and the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ z_party_name +]**</span> intends to obstruct our attempts to pass policy.
